From b305ebe54b799da7906c3d776a8fdc13cbab3567 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] Install the wavescan dictionary pcm under either ROOT naming

tools/wavescan is new in 6.4.8.0 and kept the old install rule, while the
other eight dictionary libraries were updated to accept both names. Its target
is WAVESCAN with OUTPUT_NAME wavescan, so on ROOT >= 6.40 rootcling emits
libwavescan_rdict.pcm and the install looks for libWAVESCAN_rdict.pcm:

  CMake Error at tools/wavescan/cmake_install.cmake (file):
    file INSTALL cannot find ".../libWAVESCAN_rdict.pcm"

Same treatment as wat/CMakeLists.txt and the rest.
---
 tools/wavescan/CMakeLists.txt | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tools/wavescan/CMakeLists.txt b/tools/wavescan/CMakeLists.txt
index 604dbf6..442969d 100644
--- a/tools/wavescan/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/tools/wavescan/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -41,5 +41,10 @@ ROOT_GENERATE_DICTIONARY(WAVESCAN_dict ${WAVESCAN_HDRS}
 install(TARGETS ${PROJECT_NAME})
 install(FILES ${WAVESCAN_HDRS}
         TYPE INCLUDE)
-install(FILES ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/${CMAKE_SHARED_LIBRARY_PREFIX}${PROJECT_NAME}_rdict.pcm
-        TYPE LIB)
+# ROOT names the dictionary pcm after the target OUTPUT_NAME (ROOT >= 6.40,
+# e.g. libwavescan_rdict.pcm) or after the MODULE / PROJECT_NAME (ROOT < 6.40,
+# e.g. libWAVESCAN_rdict.pcm); install whichever this ROOT emitted (OPTIONAL:
+# only one of the two names exists on any given ROOT).
+install(FILES ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/${CMAKE_SHARED_LIBRARY_PREFIX}$<TARGET_FILE_BASE_NAME:${PROJECT_NAME}>_rdict.pcm
+              ${CMAKE_CURRENT_BINARY_DIR}/${CMAKE_SHARED_LIBRARY_PREFIX}${PROJECT_NAME}_rdict.pcm
+        TYPE LIB OPTIONAL)
